WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:02.434
 Gentlemen, congratulations.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.969
The two of you have
submitted yourselves

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.239
a spot in the final
round of our competition.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.508
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:12.145
to build an iconic weapon from
history, and that weapon is--

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:17.517
 Oh, sweet.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.652
 --the Polish war hammer.

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:22.588
The Polish war hammer's
an Eastern European weapon

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:25.791
used during the 16th
and 17th centuries.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:29.028
Featuring a blunt hammer head on
one side and a sharpened spike

00:00:29.094 --> 00:00:30.797
on the other, they
were both designed

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.900
to inflict deadly blows
and piercing stabs

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.267
through an opponent's armor.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.770
It was an effective lethal
weapon used on horseback

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.072
and in hand-to-hand combat.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.073
The Polish war hammer
was a pivotal weapon

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.609
during the Battle of Vienna,
which began the decline

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.877
of the Ottoman Empire.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.045
You guys have four days.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.479
Good luck.
We'll see you then.

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:48.381
 Sweet.

00:00:53.118 --> 00:00:54.019
 I'm Mike Maldino.

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:55.221
I'm 30 years old.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.789 line:8%
I'm a high school
technology teacher

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:58.091 line:14%
and a part-time bladesmith.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.358
The thing I love
about blacksmithing

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.960
is that you're always
pushing yourself.

00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:03.630
You're always trying
to learn something new.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.131
I'm super excited to be here.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.366
It it's been a dream of mine
for a long time, but now

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:10.003
I'm working on the
hammer head billet.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.704
Everything else is
solid underneath.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.740
Now I'm going to take these two
billets down to the grinder,

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.475
and I'm going to form them
out and loose some weight.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.544
I decided I'm going
to harden and heat

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:22.147
treat the handle of the hammer
before I join the head to it.

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:23.449
It's so long and skinny.

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.751 line:8%
I'm worried about it
bending during the test.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:27.053 line:14%
Pray nothing warps.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.022 line:8%
If it twists, or
warps, or bends,

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.890
there's not much steel to
take away to straighten

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.759
it back out afterwards.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.227
All right, I'm
going to go for it.

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:41.534
Oh, straight as could be.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.335
Quench went smoothly.

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:43.870
Yeah, this came out so sweet.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.272
I'm just going to oil it up
and then give it a good test.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.041
I think we're good to go.

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:51.878
I figured we might as well
test it out on a door.

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:53.179
And it goes straight through.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.614
The head is still
firmly attached.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.783
There was no damage
to the weapon at all.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:00.986
 My name is Josh Fisher.

00:02:01.086 --> 00:02:02.488 line:14%
I'm 26 years old.

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:05.191
I've been a full time
bladesmith for over a year now.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.427
At my forge, I work with
the Wounded Warrior Project

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.329
teaching the
veterans how to make

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:13.432
knives or other
blacksmithing projects.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.402 line:8%
The biggest concern
for today is getting

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.904 line:14%
the eye of the hammer punched.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:23.042 line:8%
If the eye ends up being crooked
or doesn't punch cleanly,

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.977
then I'll never get
a good handle fit,

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.679
and it might come loose.

00:02:27.746 --> 00:02:28.982
Here we go.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.983
So getting the eye
punched went pretty good.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.251
I'm really happy with it.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.753
It's ready for the quench.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:39.458
This is really critical
for the strength of this,

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.427
and repeat that for the spike.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:51.003
See that skating on the
head, skating on that spike,

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:52.271
just what I want.

00:02:52.337 --> 00:02:55.308
We've got the hammer
almost completely done.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:58.210
Before I do all the final
cleaning and polishing on it,

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.315
I figure I'd do a
couple tasks with it.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:05.852
[inaudible] It feels great
to have made it this far.

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:08.788
It was a really tight
competition up to this point,

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:12.191
and I'd really like to
see it stay that way.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.128
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the keel test.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.596
To find out what kind of
damage your weapon will do,

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.800
I will deliver some lethal
blows on this ballistics dummy.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.836
Now I am looking to see
how your weapons will

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:27.439
crush and pierce the armor
that our ballistics dummy is

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:28.407
wearing.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.375
Joshua first.
You ready for this?

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.210
 Yep.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:47.193
 All right, Josh.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.862
First up, the handle
construction, your leather

00:03:49.928 --> 00:03:52.731
wrapping that you have here
does give me a very good grip,

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:55.835
and I'll need it because
for a one-handed weapon,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.204
it's a very heavy weapon.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:01.440
That spike penetrates
deep into the chainmail.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.576
Your hammer feet
crushes the helmet,

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.545
and it went deep into
this ballistics dummy.

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:10.450
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will keel.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.750
Mike, your turn, sir.
Are you ready?

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:12.518
 Yep.

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:13.386
 Let's do this.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:33.573
All right, Mike, first up,
your handle construction

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:35.941
is a little bit on the
blocky side for me,

00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:41.014
but your spike pierces nicely
into this ballistics dummy.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.483
Your hammerhead, the crushing
blows going to the heart

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.952
push some chainmail
into the heart.

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.287
It crushes the helmet.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:51.424
In overall, sir, it will keel.

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.862
All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test,

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:58.464
our statue smash.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.067
This test is all about
what those statues

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:04.069
do to your hammers, not what
your hammers do to the statues.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.137
Josh, you're up first.
You ready?

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:05.972
 Yep.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.788
 All right, Josh, first
off, your construction design

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:24.323
is really beautiful,
but you've taken--

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.159
abandon that head.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.093
Everything is still
tight, which is great.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.164
It's just the weight is on the
extreme side, but it held up.

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:33.599
Well done.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.233
All right, Mike.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.000
You ready?

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:35.968
 I'm ready.

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:37.002
We'll see if the hammer is.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:38.471
 Yes, we will.

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.425
All right, a couple of
things going on, Mike.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:02.128
The way these are inset,
they're actually kind of sharp,

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:06.799
so every impact, literally, you
can see a little raised spot.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.168
The Damascus pattern
is fantastic.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:11.837
The shaft's still
spot on straight.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:15.741
No damage on the spike,
but the head's loose.

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:19.145
Where this was all smooth,
I can now feel a rim.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.681
Overall, for this
test, it held up well.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:22.281
Good job.

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.116
 Thanks.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.521
 All right,
bladesmiths, this is

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:32.158
the leatherback smash and bash.

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:33.459
I'm going to take
your weapons, and I'm

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:34.961
going to see if they
can smash and bash

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:37.363
through these
double-layered leather bags.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.831
Josh, you're up first.
Are you ready for this?

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:39.432
- Yep.
- All right.

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:40.133
Let's do this.

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.315
All right, Josh.

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:57.783
You wrapped your
handle nicely so

00:06:57.849 --> 00:07:00.118
where I can have good
retention of a very

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:01.487
heavy weapon like this.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.924
That weight lends itself
to crush right inside

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.560
the bag to smash it,
and you're thick right

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.061
here penetrates deeply.

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:13.432
Overall, your weapon, it
will cut, smash, and bash,

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:15.768
or anything you want it to do.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.002
Mike, your turn, sir.
Are you ready?

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:17.937
 Yep.

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:18.971
 All right, let's do this.

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.023
All right, Mike, something
about your weapon here.

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:40.459
Initial hit, letting
the weapon do the work,

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:41.994
not so much on the impact.

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:44.730
But the lightness of your
weapon on the second strike, I

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.632
can continuously deliver
smashes and bashes

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:49.602
right into the leather bag.

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:52.705
When it comes to smashing and
bashing and maybe cutting,

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:53.272
great job.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:55.741
 Thanks.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.810
 Well, gentlemen, you
both showed your skill

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.578
and your craftsmanship
throughout the entire

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.315
competition, but
only one of you guys

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.717
is going to be leaving
here $10,000 richer,

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.752
carrying the title of
forged in fire champion.

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:12.291
Today, forged in fire
champion is Josh.

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:13.559
Congratulations.

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:14.893
You're the forged
in fire champion.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.529
Mike, unfortunately,
your hammer's not

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:17.763
coming out with the win today.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:18.965
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:08:19.065 --> 00:08:20.399
step off the forge floor.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:21.968
 Good job, man.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:23.369
 I was a little disheartened
to hear that I'm not the winner,

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:24.669
but at the same
time, I still feel

00:08:24.736 --> 00:08:26.305
like I lived up to my dream.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:29.909
I'm glad that the competition
was so tight the whole way.

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:31.110
Josh is a great guy.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.946
I look forward to seeing
what he does in the future.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:36.282
 Josh, you are the newest
forged in fire champion.

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:37.516
You're going to be
walking out of here

00:08:37.616 --> 00:08:38.917
with a check for $10,000.

00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:39.752
How do you feel?

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.587
 Amazing.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:42.855
I can't believe it.

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.523
I can't even think
of what to say.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.292
I'm just so excited.

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:51.163
This is an amazing opportunity,
and to come out of it knowing

00:08:51.263 --> 00:08:54.066
that I've won is just huge.

